hadiths[118]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3212","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas: That the funeral for which the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood was the funeral of a Jew, and the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Its smell offended me, so I stood."
"3213","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), he said: He visited a sick person, and Abu Hurayrah was with him, who had a fever. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Rejoice, for Allah says: 'It is My fire; I afflict My believing servant with it in the world so that it may be his share of the Fire in the Hereafter.'"
"3214","[AI-translation] Ala, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) visited me while I was sick, and he said: ""Rejoice, O Umm Al-Ala! For Allah removes the sins of the Muslim through his illness, just as fire removes the impurities of gold and silver."
"3215","[AI-translation] From Abu Usayb, the mawla of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), raised [to the Prophet]: Jibril came to me with fever and plague, so I held back the fever in Madinah and sent the plague to Sham. The plague is martyrdom for my Ummah, a mercy for them, and a punishment upon the disbelievers."
"3216","Al-Muttalib narrated: ""When ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn died, his funeral was brought out and he was buried. The Prophet ﷺ ordered a man to bring a stone to mark the grave, but he was unable to carry it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to it and rolled up his sleeves. Kathīr said: Al-Muttalib said: The one who informed me of this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is as if I can see the whiteness of the Messenger of Allah's forearms when he rolled them up.' Then he carried it and placed it at his head, and said: 'I mark with it my brother's grave, and I will bury next to him whoever dies from my family.'"""
"3217","[AI-translation] From Ata bin Abi Rabah, raised [to the Prophet] and mursal: ""If any one of you is afflicted with a calamity, let him remember his calamity regarding me, for it is the greatest of calamities."
"3218","[AI-translation] Bara' bin Azib, raised [to the Prophet]: ""When the believer is seated in his grave, he is approached, then he testifies that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. That is His saying: 'Allah keeps firm those who have believed, with the firm word.' He said: It was revealed regarding the punishment of the grave. (And in another narration): The Muslim, when he is questioned in the grave, testifies that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. That is His saying: 'Allah keeps firm those who have believed, with the firm word, in the worldly life and in the Hereafter.' (Ibrahim: 72)"
"3219","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""If you follow a funeral, do not sit down until it is placed (on the ground)."
"3220","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""When the believer is attended [at death], the angels of mercy come to him with a white silk shroud, and they say: 'Come out, content and pleasing [to Allah], to the spirit of Allah, a fragrant breeze, and a Lord who is not angry.' So it comes out like the finest scent of musk, until they hand it from one to another until they bring it to the gate of heaven. They say: 'How pleasant is this scent that has come to you from the earth!' Then they bring it to the spirits of the believers, and they rejoice over it more intensely than any of you rejoices when an absent loved one returns to him. They ask him: 'What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do?' They say: 'Leave him, for he was in the distress of the world.' If he says: 'Did he not come to you?' They say: 'He was taken to his mother, the Abyss [Hell].'And as for the disbeliever, when he is attended [at death], the angels of punishment come to him with a coarse cloth, and they say: 'Come out, discontent and despised, to the punishment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.' So it comes out like the most putrid stench of a corpse, until they bring it to the gate of the earth. They say: 'How foul is this scent!' Until they bring it to the spirits of the disbelievers."""
"3221","[AI-translation] From Shaddad bin Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you are present with your dying ones, close the eyes, for the sight follows the soul. And say good words, for the angels say Ameen to what the people of the household say."
"3222","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: When the believer sees what has been expanded for him in his grave, he says: ""Let me go that I may bring glad tidings to my family."" It is said to him: ""Be still."
"3223","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When one of you visits a sick person, let him say: ""O Allah, cure Your servant, that he may strike an enemy for You and walk to Your prayer."
"3224","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: Abu Musa came to visit al-Hasan ibn Ali, so Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""Have you come as a visitor or as a mourner?"" He said: ""No, rather as a visitor."" He said: So Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""If you have come as a visitor, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: When a man visits his Muslim brother, he walks in the harvest of Paradise until he sits. When he sits, he is enveloped by mercy. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning."
"3225","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When the deceased is buried — or he said: one of you — two angels come to him, black and blue-eyed. One of them is called Al-Munkar and the other An-Nakir. They say: 'What did you used to say about this man?' He says: 'What he used to say: He is Allah's servant and His Messenger. I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.' They say: 'We knew that you would say this.' Then his grave is expanded for him seventy cubits by seventy, then it is illuminated for him. Then it is said to him: 'Sleep.' He says: 'Shall I return to my family and inform them?' They say: 'Sleep like the sleep of a bridegroom whom none awakens except the most beloved of his family to him, until Allah resurrects him from that resting place of his.' And if he was a hypocrite, he says: 'I heard people saying something, so I said the like of it; I do not know.' They say: 'We knew that you would say this.' Then it is said to the earth: 'Close in on him.' So it closes in on him until his ribs interlock, and he remains therein punished until Allah resurrects him from that resting place of his."""
"3226","On the authority of Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), as a mawquf narration: When the soul of the servant is seized, the people of mercy from the servants of Allah receive him just as glad tidings are received in the world. They gather around him to question him, so some of them say to others: ""Leave your brother alone until he rests, for he was in distress."" Then they gather around him and ask: ""What became of so-and-so? What became of so-and-so (female)? Did she marry?"" If they ask about a man who died before him, he says to them: ""He has perished."" They say: ""To Allah we belong and to Him we return; he has gone to his mother, the Abyss (Hawiyah). Wretched is the mother, and wretched is the nurse."" He said: Then their deeds are presented to them. If they see good, they rejoice and are gladdened, and say: ""This is Your favor upon Your servant, so complete it."" And if they see evil, they say: ""O Allah, turn Your servant back (to the world)."""
"3227","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Masud from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: When the span of life of one of you is in a land, Allah establishes a need for him to go there. When he reaches the farthest end of his trace, He takes his soul. The earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: ""O my Lord! This is what You entrusted to me."
"3228","[AI-translation] Ashari, raised to the Prophet: When a man's child dies, Allah the Almighty says to His angels: ""Did you take the child of My servant?"" They say: ""Yes."" He says: ""Did you take the fruit of his heart?"" They say: ""Yes."" He says: ""What did My servant say?"" They say: ""He praised You and said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return."" He says: ""Build for My servant a house in Paradise and name it the House of Praise."
"3229","[AI-translation] Narrated Kab ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When one of you feels pain, let him place his hand where he feels the pain, and then let him say seven times: ""I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power over all things, from the evil of what I feel."
"3230","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Mihran that Abu Huraira said when death approached him: ""Do not pitch a tent for me, nor follow me with an incense burner, and hasten with me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: When the righteous man is placed on his bier, he says: 'Take me forward, take me forward.' And when the wicked man is placed on his bier, he says: 'O woe! Where are you taking me?'"
"3231","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: When one of you shrouds his brother, let him do it well, for they are resurrected in their shrouds and they visit one another in their shrouds."
"3232","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Remember death in your prayer, for when a man remembers death in his prayer, he is apt to perform it well. And pray the prayer of a man who does not think he will pray another prayer. And beware of every matter that requires an excuse."
"3233","[AI-translation] Narrated Ali who said: I said to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Your uncle, the old man who went astray, has died. So who will bury him?"" He said: ""Go and bury your father."" I said: ""I will not bury him, for he died as a polytheist."" He said: ""Go and bury him, but do not do anything until you come to me."" So I went and buried him, and came to him with the traces of dust and dirt on me. He ordered me to bathe, and he supplicated for me with supplications that I would be pleased to have in place of everything on earth."
"3234","[AI-translation] Narrated from Salman who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Four things from the actions of the living continue for the dead: a man who leaves a righteous offspring that prays for him, and his supplication reaches him; a man who gives an ongoing charity, for which its reward continues for him after him as long as it flows; a man who taught knowledge that is acted upon after him, so he gets the like of the reward of whoever acts upon it without anything being diminished from the reward of his action; and a man stationed on the frontier, whose action grows for him until the Day of Reckoning."
"3235","[AI-translation] Narrated from Umm Mubashshir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, entered upon me while I was in a garden of the gardens of Banu Najjar, in which there were graves of those who had died in the pre-Islamic period. He heard them while they were being punished, so he left saying: Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! Are they being punished in their graves? He said: Yes, a punishment that the beasts hear."
"3236","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurairah from the Prophet, peace be upon him: Allah has made His argument clear to a person whose lifespan He delayed until he reaches sixty years."
"3237","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: The lifespans of my Ummah are between sixty and seventy, and the fewest of them are those who exceed that."
"3238","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Jabir, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Most of those who die in my Ummah, after the Book of Allah, His decree, and His predestination, is by the souls (meaning by the eye)."
"3239","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man said to the Prophet, peace be upon him: Which of the believers is best? He said: The best of them in character. He said: Then which of the believers is most astute? He said: The most in remembering death and the best in preparing for it. Those are the astute ones."
"3240","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, passed by a people being tested, and he said: Do these not ask for well-being?"
"3241","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas bin Malik who said: I never saw anyone more merciful to dependents than the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. Ibrahim was being nursed in the outskirts of Madinah, and he used to set out and we would be with him, and he would enter the house - and indeed it would smoke, for his wet-nurse was a blacksmith - so he would take him, kiss him, and then return. (Amr said): When Ibrahim died, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Indeed, my son Ibrahim has died while nursing, and indeed he has two wet-nurses who will complete his nursing in Paradise."
"3242","[AI-translation] Rahman who said: I heard Abu Ubaydah bin Hudhayfah narrating from his paternal aunt Fatimah, who said: I visited the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, among a group of women, and there was a water skin suspended, its water dripping upon him due to the intensity of the fever he was experiencing. We said: O Messenger of Allah! If only you supplicated to Allah to remove this from you. He said: The most severely tested of the people are the Prophets, then those nearest to them, then those nearest to them."
"3243","On the authority of Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani: He went to the Mosque of Damascus early in the morning, and he met Shaddad ibn Aws and al-Sunabihi with him. I said: ""Where are you two intending, may Allah have mercy on you?"" They said: ""We intend to visit a sick brother of ours."" So I went with them until we entered upon that man. They said to him: ""How did you wake up?"" He said: ""I woke up by the blessing and favor of Allah."" Shaddad said: ""Receive glad tidings, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah the Exalted says: ""When I afflict a believing servant of Mine with a trial, and he praises Me and shows patience over what I have afflicted him with, he will rise from that bed of his as pure from sins as the day his mother gave birth to him. And the Lord says to the recording angels: 'I have confined My servant and afflicted him, so record for him the reward that you used to record for him before that, while he was healthy.'""'"""
"3244","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurairah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Verily, Allah tests His servant with illness, so that it expiates every sin from him."
"3245","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: A funeral procession passed by the Prophet and they spoke well of it, so he said: ""It is decreed."" Then another passed by and they spoke ill of it, so he said: ""It is decreed. Some of you are witnesses over others."
"3246","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Mughaffal: A man came to the Prophet and said: ""By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I love you!"" The Messenger of Allah said to him: ""Indeed, trials befall those who love me faster than a torrent to its end."
"3247","[AI-translation] Narrated Yazid bin Shajarah: The Messenger of Allah went out for a funeral, and the people spoke well and praised him well. Jibril came and said: ""The man is not as they described, but you are the witnesses of Allah on the earth, and he has been forgiven for what they do not know."
"3248","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah said: ""A man may have a rank with Allah which he cannot attain by his deeds, so Allah continues to test him with what he dislikes until He makes him reach it."
"3249","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik: The Prophet said: ""Indeed, a man intercedes for two men, and for three, and a man for a man."
"3250","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah while she had an affliction, and she said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Supplicate to Allah to heal me."" He said: ""If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah for you and He will heal you, and if you wish, be patient, and there will be no reckoning against you."
"3251","[AI-translation] Lahani: The martyrs were mentioned in the presence of Abu Anabah Al-Khawlani, and they mentioned the one with the stomach disease, the plague victim, and the woman in childbirth. Abu Anabah became angry and said: ""The companions of our Prophet narrated to us from our Prophet that he said: 'The martyrs of Allah on the earth are the trustees of Allah on the earth among His creation, whether they are killed or die.'"
"3252","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: A pain afflicted the Messenger of Allah, so he began to complain and turn over on his bed. Aishah said: ""If one of us had done this, you would have found fault with him."" The Prophet said: ""The righteous are subjected to intense trials. No believer is afflicted by a prick of a thorn or anything beyond that, except that a sin is expiated from him by it and a rank is raised for him by it."
"3253","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Umamah: The Messenger of Allah said: ""When the servant becomes ill, Allah reveals to His angels: 'O My angels, I have bound My servant with a shackle from My shackles. If I take him, I forgive him, and if I heal him, he sits with no sin on him.'"
"3254","Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi narrated from a man of his people who said: I sought the Prophet ﷺ but could not find him, so I sat down. Then I saw a group of people among whom he was, but I did not recognize him. He was reconciling between them. When he finished, some of them stood up with him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah!"" When I saw that, I said: ""Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah! Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah! Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Indeed, 'Upon you be peace' is the greeting of the dead. Indeed, 'Upon you be peace' is the greeting of the dead"" (three times). ""When a man meets his Muslim brother, let him say: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"" Then the Prophet ﷺ replied to me: ""And upon you and the mercy of Allah, and upon you and the mercy of Allah, and upon you and the mercy of Allah."""
"3255","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas from the Prophet: ""The greatness of the reward is with the greatness of the trial. And when Allah loves a people, He tests them. So whoever is pleased, for him is pleasure, and whoever is displeased, for him is displeasure."
"3256","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, marfu': ""Indeed, the grave has a squeeze. If anyone were to be saved or spared from it, Sa'd bin Mu'adh would have been saved."
"3257","[AI-translation] 'Ala bin 'Abdur-Rahman, from his father, that he witnessed a funeral over which Marwan bin Al-Hakam prayed. Abu Hurairah went with Marwan until they sat in the graveyard. Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri came and said to Marwan: ""Show me your hand."" He gave him his hand, and he said: ""Stand up,"" so he stood up. Then Marwan said to Abu Sa'id: ""Why did you make me stand up?"" He said: ""The Messenger of Allah, when he saw a funeral, would stand until it passed by, and he said: 'Indeed, death is a cause of alarm.'"" Marwan said: ""Is this true, O Abu Hurairah?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""What prevented you from telling me?"" He said: ""You were the imam, and you sat down, so I sat down."
"3258","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when death approaches the believer and he witnesses what he witnesses, he would wish for his soul to depart, and Allah loves to meet him. And the believer's soul is taken up to the heaven, and the souls of the believers come to him, asking him about their acquaintances among the people of the earth. If he says: 'I left so-and-so in the world,' they are pleased with that. And if he says: 'So-and-so has died,' they say: 'He was not brought to us.' And the believer is made to sit up in his grave and is asked: 'Who is your Lord?' He says: 'My Lord is Allah.' It is said: 'Who is your Prophet?' He says: 'My Prophet is Muhammad (peace be upon him).' It is said: 'What is your religion?' He says: 'My religion is Islam.' Then a door is opened for him in his grave, and it is said (or he is told): 'Look at your place.' Then he sees the grave, as if it were but a nap.And when death approaches the enemy of Allah and he witnesses what he witnesses, he does not wish for his soul to depart ever, and Allah hates to meet him. Then when he sits in his grave or is made to sit, it is said to him: 'Who is your Lord?' He says: 'I do not know!' It is said: 'May you never know!' Then a door from Hell is opened for him, and he is struck a blow that is heard by every creature except the two weighty ones (jinn and men). Then it is said to him: 'Sleep as the mangled one sleeps.' I said to Abu Hurayrah: 'What is the mangled one (al-manhush)?' He said: 'The one whom beasts and vermin eat away.' Then his grave constricts upon him."""
"3259","[AI-translation] From Abu 'Ubaidah bin Hudhaifah, from his paternal aunt Fatimah, that she said: We went to visit the Messenger of Allah among his wives, and there was a waterskin suspended near him, dripping its water upon him due to the severity of the heat of the fever he felt. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If only you called upon Allah to cure you."" The Messenger of Allah said: ""Indeed, the people most severely tested are the Prophets, then those closest to them, then those closest to them, then those closest to them."
"3260","[AI-translation] From Samurah, from the Prophet, that he said: ""Indeed, the best thing with which people seek medical treatment is cupping."
"3261","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, he said: I was with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar while we were waiting for the funeral of Umm Abān bint ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, and with him was ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān. Then Ibn ʿAbbās came, led by his guide. It seemed he informed him of Ibn ʿUmar's place, so he came and sat beside me, and I was between them. Then there was a sound from the house. Ibn ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Indeed the deceased is punished by the weeping of his family over him."" ʿAbdullāh narrated it as a general statement (mursalah).Ibn ʿAbbās said: We were with the Commander of the Faithful ʿUmar until, when we were at Al-Bayḍāʾ, he saw a man sitting in the shade of a tree. He said to me: ""Go and find out who that is."" So I went and found it was Ṣuhayb. I returned to him and said: ""You commanded me to find out for you who that is, and it is Ṣuhayb."" He said: ""Tell him to catch up with us."" I said: ""He has his family with him."" He said: ""Even if his family is with him."" And perhaps Ayyūb said: ""Once, to catch up with us."" When we reached Medina, the Commander of the Faithful did not stay long before he was struck (assassinated). Ṣuhayb came and said: ""O my brother! O my companion!"" ʿUmar said: ""Did you not know, or did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed the deceased is punished by some of the weeping of his family over him'?"" As for ʿAbdullāh, he narrated it as a general statement, and as for ʿUmar, he said: ""By some of the weeping...""So I came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and mentioned ʿUmar's statement to her. She said: ""No, by Allah! The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not say that the deceased is punished by the weeping of anyone! But the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed the disbeliever is increased by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in punishment by the weeping of his family over him.' (She said:) And Allah is He who causes laughter and weeping. (And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another) (Fāṭir: 18).""Ayyūb said: And Ibn Abī Mulaykah said: Al-Qāsim narrated to me: When the statement of ʿUmar and Ibn ʿUmar reached ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: ""You are narrating to me from two men who are neither liars nor accused of lying, but hearing can err."""
"3262","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas: The Prophet prayed over a deceased person three [days] after his death."
"3263","Zayd ibn Thabit said: While the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) was in a garden belonging to Banu al-Najjar, riding a mule of his, and we were with him, it shied and nearly threw him. There he found six, five, or four graves—Al-Jurayri was uncertain. He said: ""Who knows the occupants of these graves?"" A man said: ""I do."" He said: ""When did these people die?"" He said: ""They died in polytheism."" He said: ""Indeed, this nation will be tried in their graves. Were it not that you would cease burying one another, I would have asked Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave that I hear."" Zayd said: Then he turned his face towards us and said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire."" He said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."" He said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from trials, both the apparent and the hidden."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from trials, both the apparent and the hidden."" He said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the Dajjal."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the Dajjal."""
"3264","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': ""Indeed, this black seed is a cure for every disease except death."
"3265","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: I entered upon the Prophet while he was suffering from a fever. I placed my hand upon him and felt his heat between my hands above the blanket. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How severe it is upon you!"" He said: ""We are like that; the trial is doubled for us, and the reward is doubled."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Which people are most severely tested?"" He said: ""The Prophets, then the righteous. One of them would be tested with poverty until he could find nothing but the cloak he wrapped himself in. And one of them would rejoice in the trial as one of you rejoices in ease."
"3266","[AI-translation] From 'Amr bin Hazm who said: The Messenger of Allah saw me upon a grave and said: ""Step down from the grave, do not harm the companion of this grave."
"3267","[AI-translation] From Mahmud bin Labid who said: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah, died... And his eyes shed tears. They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you weep while you are the Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""I am only human; the eye sheds tears, the heart grieves, and we do not say what displeases the Lord. By Allah, O Ibrahim, we are indeed grieved for you."
"3268","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Azhar, that the Messenger of Allah said: ""The likeness of the believing servant when he is afflicted with fever or illness is like an iron rod that is entered into the fire, removing its impurities and leaving its good."
"3269","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Burdah from some of the wives of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who he thinks was 'Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, fell ill with an illness from which his distress or pain became severe. She said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, you are distressed and impatient; if a woman among us did this, she would be wondered at."" He said, ""Do you not know that the believer is subjected to severity so that it may be an expiation for his sins?"
"3270","[AI-translation] Narrated Mus'ab bin Sa'd from his father who said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Which people are most severely tested?"" He said: ""The Prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A man is tried according to the extent of (in another narration: degree of) his religion. If his religion is firm, his trial is severe, and if there is softness in his religion, he is tried according to his religion. The trial does not cease to afflict the servant until it leaves him walking upon the earth with no sin upon him."
"3271","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, went out one night, so I sent Barirah after him to see where he went. She said: He went toward Baqi' al-Gharqad and stopped at the nearest part of Baqi', then raised his hands, then turned back. Barirah returned to me and informed me. When morning came, I asked him, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Where did you go last night?"" He said: ""I was sent to the people of Baqi' to pray over them."
"3272","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Amir bin Sa'd from his father, who said: A bedouin came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: ""My father used to maintain ties of kinship, and he was such and such, so where is he?"" He said: ""In the Fire."" The bedouin seemed to find that distressing, so he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then where is your father?"" He said: ""Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him the glad tidings of the Fire."" He said: The bedouin accepted Islam after that, and he said: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, has burdened me with a task; I have not passed by the grave of a disbeliever except that I gave him the glad tidings of the Fire."
"3273","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Uthman bin 'Affan, elevated to the Prophet: Fever is the believer's share of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"3274","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Umamah, elevated to the Prophet: Fever is a bellows from Hellfire, so whatever strikes the believer from it is his share of the Fire."
"3275","[AI-translation] Khudri, elevated to the Prophet: Five, whoever does them in a day, Allah writes him among the people of Paradise: whoever visits a sick person, attends a funeral, fasts a day, goes early to Friday prayer, and frees a slave."
"3276","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, entered a palm grove of Banu al-Najjar and heard the voices of men from Banu al-Najjar who had died in the pre-Islamic period being tormented in their graves. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, came out frightened and commanded his companions to seek refuge from the punishment of the grave."
"3277","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas who said: There was an exchange of words between Khalid bin al-Walid and 'Abd al-Rahman bin 'Awf. Khalid said to 'Abd al-Rahman, ""You boast over us because of days you preceded us in?"" It reached us that this was mentioned to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: ""Leave my companions to me. By the One in Whose hand my soul is, if you spent the like of Uhud, or the like of the mountains, in gold, you would not reach their deeds."
"3278","[AI-translation] meaning Ibn 'Umar - from his father, as a mursal narration: He sprinkled water on the grave of his son Ibrahim."
"3279","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu'an: Healing is in three things: in the incision of a cupper, or a drink of honey, or cauterization by fire, and I forbid my nation from cauterization."
"3280","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, marfu'an: Two sounds are accursed: the sound of a wind instrument at a blessing, and the sound of wailing at a calamity."
"3281","[AI-translation] From Suhaib he said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was sitting with his companions, he laughed, so he said: ""Will you not ask me what makes me laugh?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What makes you laugh?"" He said: ""I marvel at the affair of the believer. Indeed, his entire affair is good. If something he loves befalls him, he praises Allah, and that is good for him. And if something he dislikes befalls him, he is patient, and that is good for him. And not every person's entire affair is good for him except the believer."
"3282","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""How wonderful is the affair of the believer! Allah does not decree anything for him except that it is good for him."
"3283","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah, the Exalted, said: ""If I test My believing servant and he does not complain about Me to his visitors, I release him from My fetters, then I replace it with flesh better than his flesh, and blood better than his blood, then he resumes his deeds."
"3284","[AI-translation] From 'Irbad bin Sariyah, marfu'an: Allah, the Exalted, said: ""If I take the precious one of My servant—while he cherishes it—I am not pleased for him with a reward less than Paradise, if he praises Me for it."
"3285","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: The Blessed and Exalted said to the soul, ""Come out."" It said, ""I will not come out except while I am unwilling."" (He said: ""Come out even if you dislike it."")"
"3286","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah he said: A funeral passed by the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, so he stood and said: ""Stand up, for death brings alarm."
"3287","[AI-translation] From Salma, the wife of Abu Rafi': When someone complained of his head, he, peace be upon him and his family, would say: ""Go and get cupped."" And when he complained of his leg, he would say: ""Go and dye it with henna."
"3288","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, marfu'an: When he complained [of illness], Jibril would perform ruqyah upon him, saying: ""In the name of Allah, He heals you, and from every disease He cures you, and from the evil of an envier when he envies, and from the evil of every possessor of an eye."
"3289","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, she said: He used to seek refuge with these words: ""O Allah, Lord of mankind, remove the harm and heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no disease."" When he became heavy in the illness in which he died, I took his hand and began to wipe him with it and say them, but he withdrew his hand from mine and said: ""O Allah, forgive me and join me with the Highest Companion."" She said: So this was the last of his speech that I heard, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him."
"3290","[AI-translation] Salt, from his uncle ('Alaqah bin Sahhar), that he passed by some people who came to him and said: ""You have come from this man with good, so treat this man for us."" They brought him a madman in shackles. He recited Umm Al-Qur'an over him for three days, morning and evening. Whenever he finished it, he would gather his saliva and then spit. It was as if he were released from a hobble. They gave him something (as payment), so he went to the Prophet, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him and his family, and mentioned it to him. The Prophet, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him, said: ""Eat, for by my life, whoever eats in payment for a false ruqyah, you have eaten in payment for a true ruqyah."
"3291","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him and his family, took a daughter of his who was dying. He embraced her and placed her between his chest, and she died while she was in front of him. Umm Ayman cried out, and it was said: ""Do you weep in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him?"" She said: ""Do I not see you weeping, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""I am not weeping; rather, it is mercy. The believer is in all good in every state; his soul exits from between his sides while he praises Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3292","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him and his family, cursed the one who scratches her face, the one who tears her collar, and the one who calls out with woe and destruction."
"3293","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him and his family, cursed the concealer and the female concealer."
"3294","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah, raising it, he said: Prompt your dying ones with ""La ilaha illa Allah,"" for the soul of the believer exits with a sweat, and the soul of the disbeliever exits from his mouth, just as the soul of a donkey exits."
"3295","[AI-translation] Bara' bin 'Azib, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a child was buried. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him, said: ""If anyone were to escape the squeeze of the grave, this child would have escaped."
"3296","[AI-translation] Madinah but found it disagreeable. He said: ""If you go out to our camels, you can drink from their urine and milk."" So they did, and they recovered. Then they attacked the shepherds, killed them, drove off the camels, and apostatized from Islam. The Prophet, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him, sent [men] in their pursuit, and they were brought. He cut off their hands and feet, gouged out their eyes, and they were left in the Harrah until they died."
"3297","[AI-translation] From Anas, that the Prophet, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him and his family, passed by a palm grove of Banu Najjar and heard a sound. He said: ""What is this?"" They said: ""A grave of a man buried in the Jahiliyyah."" The Messenger of Allah, may Allah send blessings and peace upon him and his family, said: ""Were it not that you would stop burying your dead, I would have supplicated to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to make you hear from the torment of the grave what He has made me hear."
"3298","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, raising it: Were it not for what touches it of the impurities of the Jahiliyyah, no one with a defect would touch it except that he would be healed, and there is nothing on the earth of Paradise other than it."
"3299","[AI-translation] Juhani, raised to the Prophet: There is no deed of a day except that it is sealed. When the believer falls ill, the angels say: ""O our Lord! Your servant so-and-so You have confined."" So the Lord says: ""Seal for him the like of his deed until he recovers or dies."
"3300","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, raised to the Prophet: The people of good health will wish on the Day of Resurrection that their skins were cut with shears because of what they see of the reward of the people of affliction."
"3301","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: I entered upon Umm 'Abdullah bint Abi Dhubbab visiting her during an illness, and she said: ""O Abu Hurairah! I entered upon Umm Salamah visiting her during an illness, and she looked at a sore on my hand and said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: Allah does not try a servant with a trial while he is upon a path He dislikes, except that Allah makes that trial an expiation and purification for him, as long as he does not attribute what befell him of the trial to other than Allah, or invoke other than Allah to remove it.'"
"3302","[AI-translation] From Kuraib, the mawla of 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas, who said: A son of 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas died, and he said to me: ""O Kuraib! Get up and see if anyone has gathered for my son."" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Woe to you, how many do you see... forty?"" I said: ""No, rather more."" He said: ""Then take my son out, for I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: There are not forty believers who intercede for a believer except that Allah makes them intercessors for him."
"3303","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiyah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: There is nothing that afflicts the believer in his body causing him harm, except that Allah expiates from him by it some of his sins."
"3304","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, raised to the Prophet: There is no servant who is struck by a bout of illness except that Allah resurrects him from it pure."
"3305","[AI-translation] From Muhammad bin 'Amr bin Hazm from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) that he said: There is no believer who consoles his brother for a calamity except that Allah, Glorified be He, clothes him in garments of honor on the Day of Resurrection."
"3306","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, raised to the Prophet: There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of puberty, except that Allah enters them into Paradise by the grace of His mercy upon them. And there is no Muslim who spends two pairs from his wealth in the way of Allah except that the keepers of Paradise rush to him (all of them calling him to what is before him)."
"3307","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Trial continues to afflict the believer and the believing woman in himself, his children, and his wealth until he meets Allah without having any sin upon him."
"3308","[AI-translation] Nu'man bin Bashir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer and the likeness of death is like a man who has three close friends. One of them is his wealth; he says, ""Take what you wish."" The second says, ""I am with you, and when you die, I will lower you."" The third says, ""I am with you and I will go out with you."" One of them is his wealth, the second is his family and children, and the third is his deeds."
"3309","[AI-translation] Juhani, raised: Whoever is bereaved of three from his loins and seeks their reward from Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."
"3310","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised: Whoever seeks the reward for three from his loins will enter Paradise. A woman said: ""Or two?"" He said: ""Or two."
"3311","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, raised: Whoever spends the night with the remnants of food on his hand, and something afflicts him, let him blame none but himself."
"3312","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised: Whoever prays over a funeral in the mosque, there is nothing for him."
"3313","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, raised: Whoever washes a dead person and conceals him, Allah will conceal him from sins; and whoever shrouds a Muslim, Allah will clothe him in Sundus."
"3314","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever dies upon something, Allah will resurrect him upon it."
"3315","[AI-translation] From Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, raised: The believer's sins are continually expiated."
"3316","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah, raised: The one who dies of pleurisy is a martyr."
"3317","[AI-translation] From Aisha: A Jewish woman entered upon her and mentioned the torment of the grave. She said to her: ""May Allah protect you from the torment of the grave."" Aisha then asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, about the torment of the grave. He said: ""Yes, the torment of the grave is true."" Aisha said: ""After that, I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, pray a prayer except that he sought refuge from the torment of the grave."
"3318","[AI-translation] Zubayr who said: When this verse was revealed (""Indeed, you are to die, and indeed, they are to die"" [Az-Zumar: 30]), Al-Zubayr said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will what occurs between us in this world, along with the particulars of sins, be repeated upon us?"" He said: ""Yes, it will surely be repeated upon you until every right is returned to its rightful owner."
"3319","[AI-translation] From Aishah who said: He forbade women from following funeral processions, and said: They have no reward in that."
"3320","[AI-translation] Mughirah bin Shu'bah reviled Ali bin Abi Talib. So Zaid bin Arqam stood up to him and said: O Mughirah! Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, forbade reviling the dead? So why do you revile Ali when he has died?"
"3321","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, marfu': The wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will be raised on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of pitch and a shirt of mange."
"3322","[AI-translation] From Samurah bin Jundub who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, prayed the morning prayer and said: Is anyone from Banu Fulan here? Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise due to a debt upon him."
"3323","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: The believer's illness is an expiation for his sins."
"3324","[AI-translation] Sa'ib or Umm Al-Musayyib and said: What is the matter with you, O Umm As-Sa'ib or O Umm Al-Musayyib, that you are shivering? She said: It is the fever, may Allah not bless it. He said: Do not curse the fever, for it removes the sins of the children of Adam just as the bellows remove the dross of iron."
"3325","[AI-translation] The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Do not force your sick to eat and drink, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink. Narrated from the hadith of......."
"3326","Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The person who suffered the most affliction in the world from among the people of Paradise will be brought, and it will be said: 'Dip him once in Paradise.' So he will be dipped in it once, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'O son of Adam! Did you ever see any hardship? Did you ever experience anything you disliked?' He will say: 'No, by Your Might! I never saw anything I disliked at all.' Then the person who lived the most luxurious life in the world from among the people of Hellfire will be brought, and it will be said: 'Dip him once in it.' So he will be dipped in it once, then it will be said: 'O son of Adam! Did you ever see any good? Did you ever experience any delight?' He will say: 'No, by Your Might! I never saw any good at all, nor any delight.'"""
"3327","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: I attended a funeral with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""O people! This nation will be tried in their graves. When a person is buried and his companions disperse from him, an angel comes to him with a hammer in his hand and makes him sit up. He says: 'What do you say about this man?' If he was a believer, he says: 'I testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' He says: 'You have spoken the truth.' Then a door to the Fire is opened for him, and he is told: 'This would have been your abode if you had disbelieved in your Lord; but since you believed, this is your abode.' Then a door to Paradise is opened for him, and he wants to rise up to it, but he is told: 'Be at ease!' And his grave is expanded for him. But if he was a disbeliever or a hypocrite, he is asked: 'What do you say about this man?' He says: 'I do not know; I heard the people saying something.' He is told: 'You did not know, nor did you recite, nor were you guided.' Then a door to Paradise is opened for him, and he is told: 'This would have been your abode if you had believed in your Lord; but since you disbelieved in Him, Allah has replaced it for you with this.' Then a door to the Fire is opened for him, and he is struck a blow with the hammer that is heard by all of Allah's creation except the two weighty ones (jinn and men)."" Some of the people said: ""O Messenger of Allah! No one stands with an angel over him holding a hammer but he would be bewildered at that moment."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word (in this world and the Hereafter)."" (Ibrahim: 27)"
"3328","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: When Fatimah said that—meaning when the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, experienced what he experienced from the pangs of death—Fatimah said: O my grief! The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: O my daughter! Your father is faced with that from which Allah does not spare anyone, for the meeting of the Day of Resurrection."
"3329","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Three things follow the deceased to his grave: his family, his wealth, and his deeds. Two return and one remains. His family and his wealth return, and his deeds remain."
